I edited `router.py` and wrote `NOTES.md`, but I did not run any tests. Both times I tried to run Python, it needed your approval and did not run. I checked all 32 rows in `evidence.csv` by hand, and they all came out right.

**→ What the rule does.** It changes Laya's answer to `fees_fx` only if all of these are true:
- Laya answered `disputes` or `cards`.
- The message names a rate.
- The message has a complaint word, such as "wrong", "incorrect", "bad", "take issue" or "less money than expected".

**→ What stays the same.** Every other message keeps Laya's answer. If a message names a transfer or a top-up but no card, cash or payment, it also keeps Laya's answer. That case is outside this correction.

**→ Hand check.** All 16 rate complaints change from `disputes` to `fees_fx`. None of the other 16 rows has the word "rate", so they keep Laya's answer.

**→ Known risk.** If one message has a real dispute (for example, "charged twice") and also a rate complaint, it goes to `fees_fx`.

